# Reason service (Go)

Consume `github.pr.opened`. Fetch pull body and changed files (token + User-Agent). Do not classify from title alone.

Skip-LLM is an **ordered list** (after fetch): all `.md` → `docs`; all lockfiles → `dependency-bump`. Mixed trees go to the model. Empty file list is not `docs`.

Loop: extract, then classify. Parse dirty JSON (first `{...}`), normalize labels, retry, then `unknown`. Upsert Postgres on `event_id`. Labels: `security|feature|refactor|docs|dependency-bump|unknown`.

```go
// ❌ BAD
category := "docs" // from strings.Contains(title, "readme")

// ✅ GOOD — skip-LLM on fetched file names only
if cat, ok := skipLLM(files); ok {
    return upsert(row, cat, sourceRule)
}
```

Ack after successful upsert. Postgres errors: do not ack. Enum, skip-LLM, and parse stay as functions (extension seams).

Details: `.cursor/spec/architecture.md`, `.cursor/spec/decisions.md`.
